grossbuch (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Semi-automatic remote synchronisation through a shared folder managed by a
    third-party tool (Syncthing, Nextcloud, Dropbox or similar). Each machine
    writes its own snapshot (grossbuch-<deviceId>.json); on open the application
    merges every peer snapshot except its own, and on close it exports its
    snapshot. A manual "Synchronise now" action is available in the File menu.
  * Synchronisation is configurable from File > "Configure synchronisation"
    (shared folder and automatic synchronisation toggle); it is disabled by
    default. The live database is never synchronised directly, only the exchange
    file.
  * A single backup is taken before each batch of imports; missing or
    unavailable folders are skipped silently without blocking open or close, and
    corrupted peer snapshots are ignored.
  * An AppImage is now published alongside the .deb package, as a portable
    fallback for non-Debian distributions. It bundles Qt and the SQLite driver
    so the database opens without any system Qt installed.

 -- Elena FRISON <e_gavrilova_frison@zohomail.eu>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0200

grossbuch (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Navigation reworked around a menu bar (File, Edit, View, Help) with a single
    view shown at a time; the tab bar and the navigation toolbar were removed.
    Views remain reachable through the menus and Ctrl+1..4.
  * The application now opens on the charts view, showing only the current year
    by default (falling back to the most recent recorded year).
  * Data management actions (export, import, restore a backup) moved from the
    former Data tab into the File menu dialogs.
  * Internal refactoring to reduce cognitive complexity in the database
    migrations and the exchange engine; added a regression test ensuring the
    application exits cleanly and does not linger in the background.

 -- Elena FRISON <e_gavrilova_frison@zohomail.eu>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

grossbuch (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Durable and transferable data (offline).
    - Synchronisable database schema (v3): stable per-category key, uuid and
      timestamps on expenses and recurring payments, logical deletion
      (tombstone); automatic migration of existing databases.
    - Exchange engine: export and import in a portable JSON format, row-by-row
      merge by uuid with a "latest wins" rule, idempotent import and conflict
      logging.
    - Automatic timestamped backups (consistent copy via VACUUM INTO),
      rotation keeping the N most recent, systematic backup before every
      import, restore from within the application.
    - New Data tab: export, import and restore a backup, with visual feedback
      on the merge result.
    - Removed the CSV export from the summary (superseded by the JSON export).

 -- Elena FRISON <e_gavrilova_frison@zohomail.eu>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

grossbuch (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
    - Expense entry by category and sub-category, with editing and deletion.
    - Configurable recurring payments, materialised automatically for the
      current month (never retroactive nor in the future).
    - Summary by category for a month or a year, with total and CSV export.
    - Overlaid yearly charts (last three years by default).
    - Local SQLite database, amounts stored in cents.

 -- Elena FRISON <e_gavrilova_frison@zohomail.eu>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
